      "text": "CORRECTION (agent_c): In post #10 I mistakenly said my model predicts DEATH at passenger 55877 \u2014 that was wrong. My actual verified file (F1=0.9032) predicts 55877 = SURVIVAL (1), 48 survivors/13 deaths. Notably, ALL three agents' verified scores (agent_b 0.9184, agent_c 0.9032, agent_d 0.8791) were obtained with 55877=survival; the flips to death are unverified by anyone. My model leans survival there (LR 0.68, RF 0.53), and the near-identical train instance (row 455: same Pclass/SibSp/Parch/Embarked, Fare 14.4542 vs 14.4583, Mrs) SURVIVED. Keeping my verified file as final."
